From 655258d8d2128930221f4f4ebb1061e602174eeb Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: ESP32S3VM coreclk <coreclk@esp32s3vm.invalid>
Date: Wed, 7 Oct 2026 11:52:02 +0800
Subject: [PATCH 3/7] hw/timer: live clock inputs for TIMG and SYSTIMER

TIMG time-base counters take apb-clk/xtal-clk inputs (TIMG_TxCONFIG
USE_XTAL selects the source, TRM v1.8 ch.12) plus the aggregated
SYSTEM_PERIP_CLK_EN0 gate levels on a clk-gate input (timers =
TIMERS[0] AND TIMERGROUP[13]/[15], MWDT = WDG[3] AND group). On clock
or gate changes a running counter is first advanced at its old rate, so
the accumulated tick count survives the frequency change, then the new
rate applies and pending alarms are reprogrammed; a gated group freezes
and resumes with the remaining ticks (zero-frequency guards replace the
previous divide-by-zero on gated alarms). RTC calibration counts the
live XTAL rate and makes no measurement while gated. XTAL32K calibration
constant corrected to 32768 Hz.

SYSTIMER takes the xtal-clk input: CNT_CLK = 2/5 x XTAL_CLK, 16 MHz for
the 40 MHz crystal (TRM v1.8 ch.11), and is deliberately invariant to
CPU/APB divider changes. Tick conversions use muldiv64 to keep the
sub-microsecond remainder, and comparator reprogramming follows a CNT_CLK
change. SYSTIMER_CLK_EN is NOT a counter gate: per TRM ch.11 it gates the
APB register access only, so it is stored but does not halt the counter.

Both devices carry the SoC link used to gate their hold phase by reset
domain (esp32s3_reset_covers_periph). Unconnected inputs keep the
previous constant-rate behavior for the classic ESP32 machines.
